thinking that white @ by them is just a priest until it goes swinging 
vorpal and you getting unlucky.

That scenario is one of the few times I've used life-saving on astral.  
The player monster was (wisely) on the other side of the choke point 
leading to an altar and diagonal from it and I did not notice it until I 
stepped thru.  First swing took off my head and burned an "oLS.  I think 
it got a free turn because of the "oLS action and took a few more swipes.  
I avoided the second beheading and quickly sent it away with my trusty 
wand of teleportation.  I am now much more careful to find where player 
monsters are before heading thru certain sections.

